  data: {
    LLM: 'There is no strategy in Camicia - it is a game of pure luck. The outcome is determined entirely by the order of cards in the initial deal.\n\nWhile no decisions are made during play, understanding the probabilities can be interesting. Attack cards (A, 2, 3) become diluted as you win cards, making you more vulnerable. Threes are most valuable but also most vulnerable to counterattack.\n\nNo advanced strategy exists as players make no choices. The game is mathematically deterministic based on initial card distribution.',
